C2 - Boardings and alightings
-----------------------------
known_data contains only occupancy and segment travel-time normals. There is no empirical reference for
boardings or alightings per visit, so they are NOT validated here; the IA vs AG comparison (B2) is the only
evidence. Alightings are an externally imposed calibrated input (beta-binomial), so agreement between the
models says nothing about passenger decision-making.

C3 - Segment travel times by segment x slot of the visit
--------------------------------------------------------
Times are sampled by the simulator from the same fitted normal distributions that known_data holds (plan 6, C3):
this validates the sampling and calibration procedure, not an independently learned traffic model.
MAE = mean over strata of |pooled simulated mean - empirical mean|, point +- 1.96 bootstrap SE over replicas. cover95 = share of simulated
times inside mu +- 1.96 sigma (nominal 95 % if the simulator reproduces the normal; lower where the normal has
negative support truncated/clipped by the simulator).
